{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Gerrymap</strong> is a game about <strong>gerrymandering</strong>. Your goal is to <strong>win congressional seats</strong>, not by outdated methods such as &quot;campaigning,&quot; but <strong>by drawing districts </strong>where your party's voters are in the majority!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>FEATURES</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Draw gerrymanders</strong> to aid you in your quest!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Real Census data</strong>\u00a0for <strong>1990</strong> and <strong>1992</strong>/<strong>1994</strong> election data!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Maximize gains</strong> in good election years!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Minimize losses</strong>\u00a0in bad ones!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dilute </strong>the minority vote as much as you legally can! To increase their influence, surely!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Malapportion</strong> districts\u00a0to a reasonable extent!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Connect</strong> <strong>rural and urban areas</strong> together to unite communities in this rapidly evolving, fast-paced world!</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unfortunately, the city slicker bureaucrats at the Supreme Court and Justice Department are always coming up with new, onerous<strong> </strong>requirements for us to follow. First it was &quot;One man, one vote.&quot; Now we need &quot;minority opportunity districts.&quot;</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are serious obstacles\u00a0in our way if we want to keep or even expand our House majority going into 1992. But perhaps you can do it better than the real mapmakers did?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <br><strong>INCLUDING</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The</strong> <strong>Solid South!</strong> Arkansas, Louisiana, Tennessee, Georgia, North Carolina, Florida, and Texas!</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The</strong> <strong>Democratic party!</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A GUI!</strong> (Graphical User Interface, pronounced <strong>&quot;gooey&quot;</strong>)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The first good redistricting game ever made!</strong></p></li></ul>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4120690?t=1765354683","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/279f161d45c5062425bb77b8e02a004d0c6dc506/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1765354683","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/e33e9da194e2f257f6bf34f5e8f1499e14589450/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1765354683","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/e33e9da194e2f257f6bf34f5e8f1499e14589450/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1765354683","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Camera Comfort","id":67},{"description":"Mouse Only Option","id":76},{"description":"Playable without Timed Input","id":74},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"demos":[{"appid":4187690,"description":""}],"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Gerrymap</strong> is a game about <strong>gerrymandering</strong>. Your goal is to <strong>win congressional seats</strong>, not by outdated methods such as &quot;campaigning,&quot; but <strong>by drawing districts </strong>where your party's voters are in the majority!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>FEATURES</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Draw gerrymanders</strong> to aid you in your quest!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Real Census data</strong>\u00a0for <strong>1990</strong> and <strong>1992</strong>/<strong>1994</strong> election data!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Maximize gains</strong> in good election years!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Minimize losses</strong>\u00a0in bad ones!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dilute </strong>the minority vote as much as you legally can! To increase their influence, surely!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Malapportion</strong> districts\u00a0to a reasonable extent!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Connect</strong> <strong>rural and urban areas</strong> together to unite communities in this rapidly evolving, fast-paced world!</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unfortunately, the city slicker bureaucrats at the Supreme Court and Justice Department are always coming up with new, onerous<strong> </strong>requirements for us to follow. First it was &quot;One man, one vote.&quot; Now we need &quot;minority opportunity districts.&quot;</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are serious obstacles\u00a0in our way if we want to keep or even expand our House majority going into 1992. But perhaps you can do it better than the real mapmakers did?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <br><strong>INCLUDING</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The</strong> <strong>Solid South!</strong> Arkansas, Louisiana, Tennessee, Georgia, North Carolina, Florida, and Texas!</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The</strong> <strong>Democratic party!</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A GUI!</strong> (Graphical User Interface, pronounced <strong>&quot;gooey&quot;</strong>)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The first good redistricting game ever made!</strong></p></li></ul>","developers":["Gideon Kennedy"],"genres":[{"description":"Simulation","id":"28"}],"header_image":"https://sha